bypass: 107
rule: TEST_DISABLED
title: a skip added to a pytest file kept under tests/golden/ is judged as a test beside its snapshot role
origin: issue #219 E2 (ruled 219.Q1 and 219.Q2, 2026-10-04) - v0.6.0 reported only the snapshot rule's EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED high; the same edit in tests/test_x.py reports TEST_DISABLED high
=== head: app/__init__.py ===

=== head: app/billing.py ===
def total():
    return 78.75
=== before: tests/golden/test_x.py ===
from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total() == 78.75


def test_other():
    assert total() == 78.75
=== after: tests/golden/test_x.py ===
import pytest

from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total() == 78.75


@pytest.mark.skip(reason="flaky")
def test_other():
    assert total() == 78.75
